  "status": "completed",
  "output": "The edit is in place, but I hit a wall on the byte dump:\n\n**Edit done** — one `edit_file` call, `old_string = \"retries=3\"` (1 occurrence), `new_string = \"retries=3\\ntimeout=30\"`:\n\n```\n[server]\nhost=0.0.0.0\nport=8080\n\n[client]\nretries=3\ntimeout=30\nbackoff=2\nuser_agent=acme-sync/1.4\n```\n\n**`od -c` could not run.** The bash tool refuses to execute anything here:\n\n> bash sandbox requested but unavailable on this host; refusing to run unconfined. Bubblewrap is installed but cannot create a namespace here…\n\nSo no shell command — not even read-only `od` — will run until `sandbox.bash` is turned off, which is a guarded setting only you can change. I'll point you at it rather than flip it myself.Turning `sandbox.bash` off is what unblocks the `od -c settings.ini | tail -n 6` you asked for — with it on, the host cannot create the namespace bubblewrap needs, so every command (including read-only ones) is refused. It's guarded, so I can't change it for you.\n\nOnce you've switched it off in Settings → Sandbox (or `[sandbox] bash = \"off\"` in `config.toml`), tell me and I'll run the exact command and paste its output. The file itself is already correct: `timeout=30` sits on its own line directly after `retries=3` inside `[client]`, and nothing else changed.`od` is still refused — the sandbox error is deterministic, so no command in this environment can serve as the verification the host is waiting for.Still refused — the sandbox setting hasn't taken effect yet (it may need a restart, or the toggle didn't stick). Nothing changed on my side: `settings.ini` still holds `retries=3` / `timeout=30` on adjacent lines under `[client]`.`sandbox.bash` still hasn't taken effect — the shell is refused exactly as before, so I can't produce `od -c` output yet. I also can't inspect the setting itself: the config lives outside the workspace and `/root/.config/reasonix/config.toml` is permission-denied to me.\n\n**Confirmed state of `settings.ini`** (via `read_file`, not a shell check):\n\n```\n1  [server]\n2  host=0.0.0.0\n3  port=8080\n4\n5  [client]\n6  retries=3\n7  timeout=30\n8  backoff=2\n9  user_agent=acme-sync/1.4\n```\n\nThe edit is exactly what you asked for: `timeout=30` on its own line immediately after `retries=3`, no line break consumed from `retries=3`, nothing else touched.Still waiting on you — nothing has changed on my side, and re-running the command would just hit the same refusal.\n\nTo finish the one outstanding item (`run_od`), I need you to:\n\n1. Set `[sandbox] bash = \"off\"` in `config.toml` (or Settings → Sandbox), and\n2. Restart Reasonix so the change takes effect.\n\nThen reply \"done\" and I'll immediately run `od -c settings.ini | tail -n 6` and paste its bytes, then sign off both items.\n\nThe file itself is already correct and needs no further edits: `retries=3` on line 6, `timeout=30` on line 7, inside `[client]`.",
